=== ANSWER A ===
COMMANDS RUN:
 - Skill: {"skill": "tool:skill"}
 - Bash: cat .git-blame-ignore-revs; git ls-files '*.js' '*.ts' | grep -v node_modules | wc -l; echo; echo "== surviving lines by author (ignoring reformat) =="; for f in $(git ls-files '*.js' '*.ts' | grep -v node_modules); do git blame --ignore-revs-file .git-blame-ignore-revs -w -C -M --line-porcelain "$f" | grep '^author ' ; done | sort | uniq -c | sort -rn | head -15; echo; echo "== commits (for contrast) =="; git shortlog -sn --no-merges | head -8; echo; echo "== last commit per top author =="; git log --format='%an|%ad' --date=short | awk -F'|' '!s[$1]++' | head -10
 - Bash: for f in $(git ls-files '*.js' | grep -v node_modules); do git blame --ignore-revs-file .git-blame-ignore-revs -w -C -M --line-porcelain "$f" | grep '^author ' | sort | uniq -c | sort -rn | awk -v f="$f" '{t+=$1; if(NR==1){n=$1; $1=""; a=$0}} END{printf "%s\t%d lines\t%s (%d%%)\n", f,t,a,n*100/t}'; done | sort -t$'\t' -k2 -rn | head -20; git log --format='%an' | sort | uniq -c | sort -rn | head -5
FINAL ANSWER:
**Two people own almost all of the surviving code: Troy Goode and Douglas Christopher Wilson.** I used `git blame` with the reformat commit (`62628c0`) ignored, plus `-w -C -M` to see through whitespace changes and moved or copied lines. Without that, the reformat would take credit for nearly every line.

**Lines still in the code, across 7 JS files**

| Author | Surviving lines |
|---|---|
| Troy Goode | 676 |
| Douglas Christopher Wilson | 394 |
| Alejandro Caravaca Puchades (plus alex94puchades, probably the same person) | 34 |
| Eric di Domenico | 16 |
| Alberto Leal | 15 |
| about 10 others | 9 or fewer each |

Troy Goode and Douglas Wilson together account for about 85% of the 1,200-odd lines. Commit counts alone put Wilson ahead (143 commits to Goode's 122). By surviving code, Goode owns far more.

**Ownership by file**

| File | Lines | Top owner |
|---|---|---|
| `lib/index.js` (the core) | 238 | Troy Goode, 66% |
| `test/test.js` | 731 | Douglas Wilson, 46% |
| `test/example-app.js` | 81 | Troy Goode, 82% |
| `test/error-response.js` | 66 | Troy Goode, 86% |
| `test/issue-2.js` | 48 | Troy Goode, 83% |
| `test/vary.js` | 36 | Troy Goode, 100% |
| `test/support/env.js` | 2 | Douglas Wilson, 100% |

**Bus factor**
- The project-level bus factor is **2**. Losing Goode and Wilson would leave nobody who wrote most of the code.
- `lib/index.js` is the riskiest file because it's the core. Goode wrote two-thirds of what's still there, and the rest is spread thinly across others.
- `test/vary.js` is a single-author file (Goode, 100%), but it's small and low-impact.
- Wilson's share is mostly in `test/test.js`, where his 46% is the largest block but not a majority.

**Activity**
- The latest commit by anyone is from 2026-04-12 (Fiona Formatter), and Goode's last commit is 2026-04-10. Both are about six months before today (2026-10-24).
- I only pulled last-commit dates for the 10 most recent committers. Wilson wasn't among them, so I haven't checked whether he's still active. Every author in that list last committed more than 90 days ago.

**Caveats**
- I didn't run the skill's importance cross-check (how many files import each one) or the contributor-analyzer agent. With only 7 source files, the per-file table covers the same ground.
- The 7-file count covers tracked `.js` and `.ts` files only.
- Blame can't tell a line someone wrote from one they moved or copied unchanged, so a few lines may be credited to the wrong person.

**Recommendation:** have someone other than Goode review or pair on `lib/index.js` changes, and spread `test/test.js` ownership beyond Wilson.
